# promise: crash-webstore-install-double-report
# An imported extension's copy loads again (here it reloads itself, 3 s in) while Cra's install of it from the
# Web Store is still under way. Chrome's WebstoreInstaller took any install of the ID for its own: it reported
# success for the copy, Cra let go of the install's page, and the store install's next step, finding the page gone,
# reported a failure on top: CHECK(failure_callback_) stopped Cra (0.1.48 crash report, 18 Nov 2026: the
# --load-extension copy finished loading after the first page). Only the store's own install (INTERNAL) is its success
# now, and a second report does nothing: the store's answer, a late 404, is what Cra hears.
budget rss=700
extension ${FIXTURES}/WebStoreReloadCopy/baekfgaggmimgflkhoiihmcpnockmmdl
# The store's download answers 404, ten seconds late: the copy reloads in that time.
arg --apps-gallery-download-url=${ORIGIN}/missing/%s.crx?delay=10
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=store
expect-log extension baekfgaggmimgflkhoiihmcpnockmmdl: installing from the Web Store in Default
wait 13
expect-log GET /missing/baekfgaggmimgflkhoiihmcpnockmmdl
expect-log Web Store install in Default failed
